   "evidence": "Outer.lean:174-178 `have hz : z \u2022 \ud835\udfd9 M = ObjectProperty.homMk (ModuleCat.ofHom (Module.End.smulLeft (z : A) z.property)) := by ext m; rfl`; Outer.lean:97-102 `have hscalar : ... = r \u2022 \ud835\udfd9 M := by ext m; rfl`. `ModuleCat.Algebra.instLinear` is only a local instance here (line 74), so consumers can reach this fact only through a fresh defeq argument.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/DerivationExtension/Outer.lean",
   "fix": "Export one public lemma for central scalars on discrete modules, e.g. `center_smul_id_eq_homMk_smulLeft (z : Subalgebra.center R A) (M) : z \u2022 \ud835\udfd9 M = ObjectProperty.homMk (ModuleCat.ofHom (Module.End.smulLeft (z : A) z.property))`. Also expose its Ext corollary `z \u2022 e = e.comp (Ext.mk\u2080 (\u2026smulLeft z\u2026)) (add_zero _)`. Use them at line 174 and derive the `R` case at line 97 from them, rather than repeating `rfl` proofs.",
   "issue": "The equation `z \u2022 \ud835\udfd9 M = ObjectProperty.homMk (ModuleCat.ofHom (Module.End.smulLeft (z : A) z.property))` is the only link between the new `Subalgebra.center R A`-linear structure and the concrete endomorphism, yet it is an inline `have` proved by `rfl` through instance unfolding. The PR says it identifies central multiplication on native Ext, but it exports no such lemma. The same fact for `R` is duplicated as `hscalar` at line 97. R5.2 consumers composing \u03b8 with this map, or computing `z \u2022 e` on Ext, must re-prove it by defeq.",
   "line": 174
  }
